.SH "NAME"
aerospace-list-windows \- Print windows that satisfy conditions
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
aerospace list\-windows [\-h|\-\-help] (\-\-workspace <workspace>...|\-\-monitor <monitor>...)
                       [\-\-monitor <monitor>...] [\-\-workspace <workspace>...]
                       [\-\-pid <pid>] [\-\-app\-bundle\-id <app\-bundle\-id>] [\-\-format <output\-format>]
                       [\-\-count] [\-\-json]
aerospace list\-windows [\-h|\-\-help] \-\-all [\-\-format <output\-format>] [\-\-count] [\-\-json]
aerospace list\-windows [\-h|\-\-help] \-\-focused [\-\-format <output\-format>] [\-\-count] [\-\-json]
.fi
.br
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Print windows that satisfy conditions
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help
.RE
.sp
\-\-all
.RS 4
Alias for \f(CR\-\-monitor all\fP.
Please use this option \fBwith caution\fP.
Use it when you really need to get workspaces/windows from \fBall monitors\fP.
.sp
For multi\-monitor setup \f(CR\-\-monitor focused\fP is almost always a preferred option.
If you\(cqre automating something then you don\(cqt want to mess up with workspaces/windows on a different monitor.
.sp
With great power comes great responsibility.
.RE
.sp
\-\-focused
.RS 4
Print the focused window.
Please note that it is possible for no window to be in focus.
In that case, error is reported.
.RE
.sp
\-\-workspace <workspace>...
.RS 4
Filter results to only print windows that belong to either of specified workspaces.
\f(CR<workspace>...\fP is a space\-separated list of workspace names.
.sp
Possible values:
.br
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 1." 4.2
.\}
Workspace name
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 2." 4.2
.\}
\f(CRfocused\fP is a special workspace name that represents the focused workspace
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 3." 4.2
.\}
\f(CRvisible\fP is a special workspace name that represents all currently visible workspaces (In multi\-monitor setup, there are multiple visible workspaces)
.RE
.RE
.sp
\-\-monitor <monitors>
.RS 4
Filter results to only print workspaces/windows that are attached to specified monitors.
\f(CR<monitors>\fP is a space separated list of monitor IDs.
.br
.sp
Possible monitors IDs:
.br
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 1." 4.2
.\}
1\-based index of a monitor as if monitors were ordered horizontally from left to right
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 2." 4.2
.\}
\f(CRall\fP is a special monitor ID that represents all monitors
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 3." 4.2
.\}
\f(CRmouse\fP is a special monitor ID that represents monitor with the mouse
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 4." 4.2
.\}
\f(CRfocused\fP is a special monitor ID that represents the focused monitor
.RE
.RE
.sp
\-\-pid <pid>
.RS 4
Filter results to only print windows that belong to the Application with specified \f(CR<pid>\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-app\-bundle\-id <app\-bundle\-id>
.RS 4
Filter results to only print windows that belong to the Application with specified \c
.URL "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appstoreconnectapi/bundle_ids" "Bundle ID" ""
.sp
Deprecated (but still supported) flag name: \f(CR\-\-app\-id\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-format <output\-format>
.RS 4
Specify output format. See "Output Format" section for more details.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-count
.RS 4
Output only the number of windows.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-format\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-json
.RS 4
Output in JSON format.
Can be used in combination with \f(CR\-\-format\fP to specify which data to include into the json.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
.sp
Output format can be configured with optional \f(CR[\-\-format <output\-format>]\fP option.
\f(CR<output\-format>\fP supports \c
.URL "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_interpolation" "string interpolation" "."
.sp
If not specified, the default \f(CR<output\-format>\fP is:
.br
\f(CR%{window\-id}%{right\-padding} | %{app\-name}%{right\-padding} | %{window\-title}\fP
.sp
The following variables can be used inside \f(CR<output\-format>\fP:
.sp
%{window\-id}
.RS 4
Number. Window unique ID
.RE
.sp
%{window\-title}
.RS 4
String. Window title
.RE
.sp
%{window\-is\-fullscreen}
.RS 4
Boolean. Is window in fullscreen by \f(CRaerospace fullscreen\fP command
.RE
.sp
%{window\-layout}
.RS 4
String. Alias for \f(CR%{window\-parent\-container\-layout}\fP
.RE
.sp
%{window\-parent\-container\-layout}
.RS 4
String. The layout (\f(CRv_tiles\fP, \f(CRh_tiles\fP, \f(CRv_accordion\fP, \f(CRh_accordion\fP, \f(CRfloating\fP) of the window\(cqs parent container.
.RE
.sp
%{app\-bundle\-id}
.RS 4
String. Application unique identifier. \c
.URL "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appstoreconnectapi/bundle_ids" "Bundle ID" ""
.RE
.sp
%{app\-name}
.RS 4
String. Application name
.RE
.sp
%{app\-pid}
.RS 4
Number. \c
.URL "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Process_identifier" "UNIX process identifier" ""
.RE
.sp
%{app\-exec\-path}
.RS 4
String. Application executable path
.RE
.sp
%{app\-bundle\-path}
.RS 4
String. Application bundle path
.RE
.sp
%{workspace}
.RS 4
String. Name of the belonging workspace
.RE
.sp
%{workspace\-is\-focused}
.RS 4
Boolean. True if the workspace has focus
.RE
.sp
%{workspace\-is\-visible}
.RS 4
Boolean. True if the workspace is visible. A workspace can be visible but not focused in a multi\-monitor setup
.RE
.sp
%{workspace\-root\-container\-layout}
.RS 4
String. The layout (\f(CRv_tiles\fP, \f(CRh_tiles\fP, \f(CRv_accordion\fP, \f(CRh_accordion\fP) of the workspace the window belongs to.
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-id}
.RS 4
1\-based Number. Sequential number of the belonging monitor.
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-appkit\-nsscreen\-screens\-id}
.RS 4
1\-based index of the belonging monitor in \f(CRNSScreen.screens\fP array. Useful for integration with other tools that might be using \f(CRNSScreen.screens\fP ordering (like sketchybar).
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-name}
.RS 4
String. Name of the belonging monitor
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-is\-main}
.RS 4
Boolean. True if the monitor is main.
.RE
.sp
%{right\-padding}
.RS 4
A special variable which expands with a minimum number of spaces required to form a right padding in the appropriate column
.RE
.sp
%{newline}
.RS 4
Unicode U+000A newline symbol \f(CR\(rsn\fP
.RE
.sp
%{tab}
.RS 4
Unicode U+0009 tab symbol \f(CR\(rst\fP
.RE
